*> --------------------------------------------------------------------
*> Program : STUDENT-MARK
*> Author  : Rekhashanmuganathan
*> Date    : 2026-08-04
*> Version : 1.1
*> Purpose : Calculate total and average marks for a student across
*>           three subjects. This version follows basic COBOL coding
*>           standards and includes inline documentation and improved
*>           naming for readability and maintainability.
*> --------------------------------------------------------------------

       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. STUDENT-MARK.
       * Optional author/date information
       AUTHOR. Rekhashanmuganathan.
       INSTALLATION. SampleTestTraining.
       DATE-WRITTEN. 2026-08-04.

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.

       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

       *> Working storage for student record and calculations
       01  WS-STUDENT-RECORD.
           05  WS-STUDENT-NAME     PIC X(20) VALUE "RAJESH".
           05  WS-SUB1             PIC 9(3)  VALUE 85.
           05  WS-SUB2             PIC 9(3)  VALUE 90.
           05  WS-SUB3             PIC 9(3)  VALUE 78.
           05  WS-TOTAL            PIC 9(4)  VALUE 0.
           05  WS-AVG              PIC 9(3)V99 VALUE 0.

       *> Edited field for human-readable average (shows decimal point)
       01  WS-EDITED-FIELDS.
           05  WS-AVG-ED           PIC ZZZ.99.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-PROCEDURE.
           *> Compute total marks from individual subject marks
           COMPUTE WS-TOTAL = WS-SUB1 + WS-SUB2 + WS-SUB3

           *> Compute average. Use ROUNDED to handle fractions properly
           COMPUTE WS-AVG = WS-TOTAL / 3 ROUNDED

           *> Move numeric average to an edited field so the decimal
           *> point is visible when displayed
           MOVE WS-AVG TO WS-AVG-ED

           *> Display results with clear labels and consistent formatting
           DISPLAY "--------------------------------------------------"
           DISPLAY "STUDENT NAME : " WS-STUDENT-NAME
           DISPLAY "SUBJECT 1     : " WS-SUB1
           DISPLAY "SUBJECT 2     : " WS-SUB2
           DISPLAY "SUBJECT 3     : " WS-SUB3
           DISPLAY "--------------------------------------------------"
           DISPLAY "TOTAL MARKS   : " WS-TOTAL
           DISPLAY "AVERAGE       : " WS-AVG-ED
           DISPLAY "--------------------------------------------------"

           *> Normal program termination
           STOP RUN.

       * End of program
